<questestinterop xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/ims_qtiasiv1p2" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/ims_qtiasiv1p2 http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/ims_qtiasiv1p2p1.xsd">
<assessment ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157" title="Unit 8 Check: Road to Revolution"><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>cc_maxattempts</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata><section ident="root_section">
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1" title="Question 1"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Britain won the French and Indian War in 1763. What happened next?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Britain gave the colonies seats in Parliament and a vote on taxes.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">France took control of the thirteen colonies and ruled them from Paris.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Britain had a large war debt, so Parliament taxed the colonies.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Britain stopped collecting taxes in the colonies for ten years.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q1_a3</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. Winning the war left Britain deep in debt, so Parliament looked to the colonies to help pay it. Britain also drew the Proclamation Line of 1763 and told colonists not to settle west of it.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.01. Britain won the war but came out of it with a large debt, and new taxes followed.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2" title="Question 2"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Colonists said “No taxation without representation.” What did they mean?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">They had no elected members in Parliament.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">They thought all taxes were wrong, anywhere in the world.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">They wanted France to collect the taxes instead of Britain.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">They thought only rich colonists should pay any taxes.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q2_a1</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. Parliament taxed the colonists, but no colonist had been elected to sit in it and argue for them.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.02. The argument was about who gets a say, not about whether taxes should exist.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3" title="Question 3"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Some colonists took neither side in the argument about independence. What were they called?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Patriots</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Loyalists</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Neutral</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Ministers</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q3_a3</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. Neutral means taking neither side, and it was a large group — roughly a third of colonists.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.03. Patriots wanted independence and Loyalists wanted to stay British. Neutral colonists chose neither.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4" title="Question 4"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The Declaration of Independence says people have unalienable rights. What does unalienable mean?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Given only to leaders</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Able to be bought</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Written down in law</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Cannot be taken away</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q4_a4</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. The Declaration argues people are born with these rights, so no government can take them away.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.04. Unalienable rights are rights nobody can take from you.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5" title="Question 5"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The Declaration said “all men are created equal.” Which statement about 1776 is accurate?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Those words gave the same rights to everyone living in the colonies.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Enslaved people, women and Native nations did not get those rights.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The words were added to the Declaration a hundred years later.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Only the men who signed the Declaration were covered by the words.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q5_a2</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. The words were powerful, and they did not reach everyone in 1776. People used them later to argue for rights they had been denied.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.04. The idea was bigger than what the law actually did in 1776.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6" title="Question 6"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_answers_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Which of these helped the American Revolution? Choose every right answer.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Multiple"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Haym Salomon, who raised money to pay for the war</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Wentworth Cheswell, who rode to warn colonists and served as a soldier</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The First Rhode Island Regiment, which included Black and Native soldiers</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Captain Thomas Preston, who commanded the British soldiers in Boston</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><and><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a1</varequal><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a2</varequal><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a3</varequal><not><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q6_a4</varequal></not></and></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. The Revolution ran on a wide group of people: someone had to pay for it, carry warnings and fight.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.05. Salomon, Cheswell and the First Rhode Island Regiment all worked for the Revolution. Captain Preston commanded British soldiers.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7" title="Question 7"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Historians have written records showing Deborah Sampson served as a soldier. For “Molly Pitcher” they have stories but no such records. What should a careful historian say?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Sampson’s service is documented; Molly Pitcher is partly legend.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Both stories rest on exactly the same kind of evidence.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Neither woman did anything during the Revolution at all.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">A good story is stronger evidence than a written record.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q7_a1</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. Documented means there are records. Saying so honestly is not the same as saying the legend is worthless.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.06. One of these has records behind it and one does not, and a careful historian says which is which.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8" title="Question 8"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>matching_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Match each change to what it did.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The 15th Amendment (1870)</mattext></material><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">A man could not be kept from voting because of his race</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Women could not be kept from voting because they are women</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The voting age dropped from 21 to 18</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Everyone in the country could vote for the first time</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid><response_lid ident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The 19th Amendment (1920)</mattext></material><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">A man could not be kept from voting because of his race</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Women could not be kept from voting because they are women</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The voting age dropped from 21 to 18</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Everyone in the country could vote for the first time</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid><response_lid ident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The 26th Amendment (1971)</mattext></material><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">A man could not be kept from voting because of his race</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Women could not be kept from voting because they are women</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The voting age dropped from 21 to 18</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Everyone in the country could vote for the first time</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition><conditionvar><varequal respident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m1</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Add" varname="SCORE">33.33</setvar></respcondition><respcondition><conditionvar><varequal respident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a2">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m2</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Add" varname="SCORE">33.33</setvar></respcondition><respcondition><conditionvar><varequal respident="response_g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_a3">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q8_m3</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Add" varname="SCORE">33.33</setvar></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. The vote widened one step at a time, and people had to push for every step.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.07 and the year slider: 1870 was about race, 1920 about women, 1971 about age.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9" title="Question 9"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Two packets about the night of 5 March 1770 were both printed in 1770. One calls it an “unhappy disturbance.” The other calls it a “horrid massacre.” What does that show?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">One packet was printed many years after the other one.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Only one of the two packets was really printed in 1770.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The two packets agree about everything that happened.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">Two sources about one event can describe it very differently.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q9_a4</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. Both were printed close to the event, and they still disagree. Being close to an event does not make a source complete.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.08. Both title pages are dated 1770 — the difference is in the words each side chose.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
<item ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10" title="Question 10"><itemmetadata><qtimetadata><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel><fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel><fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield><qtimetadatafield><fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel><fieldentry>g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a1,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a2,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a3,g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a4</fieldentry></qtimetadatafield></qtimetadata></itemmetadata><presentation><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;John Adams was a Patriot. In 1770 he defended the British soldiers in court. Why?&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material><response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"><render_choice><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a1"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">He had changed sides and become a Loyalist.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a2"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">He believed every person deserves a fair trial.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a3"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">The king had ordered him to take the case.</mattext></material></response_label><response_label ident="g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a4"><material><mattext texttype="text/plain">He wanted the soldiers to be found guilty.</mattext></material></response_label></render_choice></response_lid></presentation><resprocessing><outcomes><decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/></outcomes><respcondition continue="No"><conditionvar><varequal respident="response1">g5u08quizb9d6c9fd8bef800ed157_q10_a2</varequal></conditionvar><setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="correct_fb"/></respcondition><respcondition continue="Yes"><conditionvar><other/></conditionvar><displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="general_incorrect_fb"/></respcondition></resprocessing><itemfeedback ident="correct_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Right. He stayed a Patriot. He took the case because he thought a fair trial mattered more than which side you were on.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback><itemfeedback ident="general_incorrect_fb"><flow_mat><material><mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Look back at 5.08.08. Adams did not change sides, and he was not ordered to do it.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext></material></flow_mat></itemfeedback></item>
</section></assessment>
